Read `development/00-project-status.md` for the current plan, maturity and open work.
All ordered electronics are reported received; that does not establish a physical PASS.
Use `development/bench-prep/README.md` for the current bench setup.
The full field schematic/controller remains in development. A custom PCB is optional;
the current recommendation is a qualified, enclosed modular assembly.
Read the relevant files before changing connections. This repository's older
Phase 1 wiring and recently simplified direct-pin sketch are different baselines.

- User reports Uno D5, D6 and D7 faulty. Leave them disconnected. An MCP23017
  adds digital I/O but does not establish the health of the remaining Uno.
- Known bench wiring is in `development/bench-prep/design.json`, its generated
  wire schedule, and the matching native KiCad schematic. References are local
  to each separate project. Match physical silkscreen, not box orientation.
- Stage 1 loopback uses only Uno USB 5V/GND/A4/A5 and DFR0627 T/R loops.
  Remove loopbacks before the separate RS485 logic harness. No Uno Serial1
  exists on this Uno R3; use the DFR0627 library for that extra UART.
- Stage 2 GPIO input board 5346 is 0x21; optional 6318 remains 0x20 with V+
  and all load terminals unconnected. MCP A7/B7 are not changing inputs.
- Uno A0/A1/A2 drive only resistor/LED branches. Expander A0/A1/A2 are distinct
  digital pins, not Uno analog pins. Never map them using plain digitalRead(5).
- All bench sensor contacts are simulated. Do not connect powered field
  sensors, gauge analog outputs, 24V terminals, coils, pumps or pilots to them.
- Field terminals, Hornet firmware/protocol, coil ratings, pneumatic failure
  behavior and pressure limits must come from matched OEM sources/measurements.
  Preserve unresolved items in `06-field-holds.md`; never guess to finish a task.
- Reconcile design.json, pin map, firmware, native schematics, wire schedule
  and checks for a connection change. Generator overwrites generated files.
- Use `tools/validate_package.py --kicad` after changes. Inspect native renders.
  Passive interface symbols are not simulation models or electrical qualification.
- Keep bench-only scope explicit. No physical PASS unless actually measured.
- Use small standalone controller firmware; laptop/UI requests cannot bypass
  permissions. Preserve existing lab machine interlocks and qualified close paths.
- Cursor may guide GUI actions and edit files/run CLI when locally available.
  Do not claim desktop control, hardware access or a plugin that is not present.
- Teach one action at a time with its reason and expected observation. Prefer
  the supplied project over making a beginner manually place every symbol.

Primary GUI, CLI, component and library sources are indexed in
`development/bench-prep/resources/source-register.json`. Read only the section
needed for the current action; do not ingest whole manuals as a substitute for
checking the actual terminal map.
